# Page Objects

- One class per page/screen; export class; constructor stores `page`.
- Locators in constructor: prefer `getByRole` / accessible names over CSS/XPath.
- Actions are methods; assertions use Playwright `expect` on locators.
- **No credentials** in page objects — callers pass data from `test-data/` / fixtures.
- Reuse existing page methods; do not duplicate login or master-create flows in new pages.
- Keep methods focused (fill, submit, search, cancel); avoid giant god-methods unless matching `e2eWorkflow` helpers.

```js
// Prefer
this.nameInput = page.getByRole('textbox', { name: 'Client Name' });

// Avoid brittle selectors unless no accessible name exists
this.nameInput = page.locator('#client-name-xyz');
```
